<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim al-Hamdi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943–1977</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim al-Hamdi (1943–1977) was president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> Arab Republic (North Yemen) from 1974 to 1977. He came to power in a bloodless military coup, curbed the power of the tribal sheikhs, promoted development through local cooperatives and sought closer ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>. He was assassinated in Sanaa in October 1977, shortly before a planned visit to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibrahim-al-hamdi.jpg" alt="Ibrahim al-Hamdi" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ibrahim_al-Hamdi_during_parade_of_the_Yemen_Arab_republic%27s_army.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
